# <binary> <test or *> <mode> <reason>
# binary: a --test target name, lib (library unit tests) or bin-<name> (that binary's unit tests)
# mode: run-bin (only with *: the cargo bin <binary> itself runs under memcheck; the rest of the line is its argument list) | skip (not run under memcheck) | api-errors-no (run alone with --report-api-errors no) | no-cuda (only with *: the binary runs and must make no CUDA call)
#       | no-cuda-app-only (only with *: as no-cuda, run with --target-processes application-only; for a binary whose child processes make no CUDA call either)
# An api-errors-no test is still memchecked; only driver API error reporting is off, for that test only.
gpu_memory_plan a_refused_device_allocation_is_reported_with_its_bytes api-errors-no  provokes a cudaMalloc out-of-memory on purpose
gpu_ring        stale_cuda_error_does_not_fail_the_transport           api-errors-no  provokes a cudaMalloc out-of-memory on purpose
gpu_launch_guard malloc_argument_is_refused_before_the_kernel_runs       api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard stack_argument_is_refused                               api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard pinned_argument_is_refused                              api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard by_value_struct_with_a_host_member_is_refused           api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard opt_out_disables_the_check                              api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_refusal_cli explicit_gpu_run_fails_closed_when_a_launch_is_refused  api-errors-no  forces a launch refusal on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_refusal_cli auto_dispatch_falls_back_to_the_cpu_with_the_cause_and_the_cpu_archive api-errors-no  forces a launch refusal on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
# no-cuda: the binary makes no CUDA call by design and must keep it. A pass at rc 255 (terminated before first instrumented API call) is accepted only for a listed binary.
# A listed binary that calls CUDA gets the normal memcheck verdict and the summary marks it; an unlisted binary with rc 255 fails the pass.
attach                 *  no-cuda  its tests are ignored (measurement or external data): 0 tests run and none calls CUDA
bin-cpu_bench          *  no-cuda  no tests in this binary: the harness runs 0 tests and makes no CUDA call
bin-rcsr               *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
bin-rcsr-bench         *  no-cuda  no tests in this binary: the harness runs 0 tests and makes no CUDA call
bin-rcsr-gpu-bench     *  skip     no tests in this binary: the harness runs 0 tests; the binary itself runs on the rcsr-gpu-bench line
bin-rcsr-launch        *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
bin-rcsr-rss           *  no-cuda  no tests in this binary: the harness runs 0 tests and makes no CUDA call
bin-rcsr_serve         *  no-cuda  no tests in this binary: the harness runs 0 tests and makes no CUDA call
conflict_markers       *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
cpu_bench              *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
cuda_kernel_args       *  no-cuda  text lint of src/cuda sources; no CUDA call
cv                     *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
derivatives            *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
diagnostics            *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
dispatch_cli           *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
eval_soa               *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
fit_portfolio          *  no-cuda  CPU fits and a mock GPU fitter; no CUDA call
fit_portfolio_bench    *  no-cuda  its tests are ignored (measurement or external data): 0 tests run and none calls CUDA
fit_stream_store       *  no-cuda  CPU-only tests; no CUDA call
